# Model Context Protocol (MCP) Integration Guidelines

## Overview
MCP is used to connect the Angband variant with local LLMs via Ollama for dynamic gameplay generation.

## Server Configuration
- Default port: 11434 (Ollama default)
- Backup port: 8000 (if Ollama port is unavailable)
- Connection timeout: 5 seconds
- Retry attempts: 3

## Model Selection
- Primary: `codellama:13b` - For code generation and game logic
- Secondary: `llama2:13b` - For narrative and world building
- Fallback: `mistral:7b` - For lightweight interactions

## Context Management
- Game state context: Limited to 4000 tokens
- Player history context: Limited to 2000 tokens
- World state context: Limited to 2000 tokens
- Lore context: Limited to 2000 tokens

## MCP Endpoints

### Companion System
- `ages/companion/dialogue`: Generate dialogue for a companion
  - Parameters: companion_name, age, topic (optional), relationship_level
  - Response: dialogue, companion, age, topic

- `ages/companion/info`: Get information about a companion
  - Parameters: companion_name, age
  - Response: companion data including background, traits, and relationships

- `ages/relationship/update`: Update the relationship level with a companion
  - Parameters: companion_name, change_amount, reason
  - Response: new_level, companion_name, reaction

### Lore System
- `ages/lore/character`: Get character lore
  - Parameters: character_name, age (optional)
  - Response: content, source, age, year, is_canonical

- `ages/lore/location`: Get location lore
  - Parameters: location_name, age (optional)
  - Response: content, source, age, year, is_canonical

- `ages/lore/artifact`: Get artifact lore
  - Parameters: artifact_name, age (optional)
  - Response: content, source, age, year, is_canonical

- `ages/lore/random`: Get random lore
  - Parameters: topic_type (optional), age (optional)
  - Response: content, topic_type, age, source

- `ages/lore/age/set`: Set the current age
  - Parameters: age
  - Response: status, age

- `ages/lore/age/get`: Get the current age
  - Parameters: none
  - Response: age

### Narrative Generation
- `ages/narrative/location`: Generate location description
  - Parameters: location_name, age, context (optional)
  - Response: description, location, age

- `ages/narrative/companion`: Generate companion dialogue
  - Parameters: companion_name, age, topic (optional), relationship_level, context (optional)
  - Response: dialogue, companion, age, topic

- `ages/narrative/quest`: Generate quest
  - Parameters: quest_type, location, age, target (optional), context (optional)
  - Response: title, description, quest_type, location, age, target

### Timeline Management
- `ages/timeline/info`: Get information about the current timeline
  - Parameters: none
  - Response: current_age, year, major_events

- `ages/player/death`: Handle player death and advance the timeline
  - Parameters: cause_of_death, player_level, achievements
  - Response: new_age, new_year, new_companion, death_narrative

## Prompt Templates
```
[GAME_STATE]
{game_state_json}
[/GAME_STATE]

[PLAYER_HISTORY]
{player_history_text}
[/PLAYER_HISTORY]

[WORLD_STATE]
{world_state_json}
[/WORLD_STATE]

[LORE_CONTEXT]
{relevant_lore_json}
[/LORE_CONTEXT]

[INSTRUCTION]
{specific_instruction}
[/INSTRUCTION]
```

## Response Parsing
- JSON format expected for structured data
- Plain text for narrative responses
- Error handling for malformed responses
- Validation against lore accuracy when applicable

## Performance Considerations
- Cache common responses
- Batch similar requests
- Use async processing for non-blocking gameplay
- Implement fallback behavior for offline play
- Prioritize template-based generation for time-sensitive operations

## Security
- No sensitive data in prompts
- Sanitize all LLM outputs before processing
- Implement rate limiting
- Local-only deployment by default

## Testing
- Mock LLM responses for unit tests
- Benchmark response times
- Validate response formats
- Verify lore accuracy and consistency 